WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.080
to low, double-digit growth range.

00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.280
So that's been positive overall, I think.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.400
But there's no question it won't get back to the really high growth rates

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.760
we saw a few years ago.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.320
We also see a higher number of competitors entering in each segment as well,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.080
which is something we have to just be ready for when we do launch in China.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:23.080
Nonetheless, very large market, highly attractive,

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.520
and I think you've seen the strong performance that we've had.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.560
You know, I think for Lecveo, we have guided that Entresto, Cosentix,

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:34.400
we've guided that Entresto can be a billion-dollar medicine across its indications.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.720
And certainly, we have the aspiration to make Lecveo as big or bigger than Entresto over time.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.520
It's early days, I think, understanding the trajectory of how we get there.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.200
But I would say we see very solid demand for the medicine,

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:54.660
and I think if we could make it in the range of Entresto, that would be a success.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.400
Thank you.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.800
Your next question comes from the line of Simon Baker from Rothschild.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.440
Please go ahead.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.360
Thank you very much for taking my question, and I will stick to the one.

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:14.400
Taking up on your offer, Vaz, could you give us your updated levels of confidence

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.600
on the timing and outcome of the Pellicast and Horizon study?

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.160
Thanks so much.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:21.680
Yes, Simon.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.640
So I don't think I have anything new to add, unfortunately,

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.000
because we don't have any new information.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.560
But I think we, of course, continue to make sure that the studies,

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.000
the studies on track, no change in our expected readout.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.080
We do expect a readout in the early part of the second half of the year.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.840
So no change with respect to that.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:50.360
I think if we get a positive result overall, that regardless of the relative risk reduction,

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.280
we'll find a way to ultimately launch the medicine.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.520
I think what we'll be really looking for is are there either the 90 milligram

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:03.240
pre-specified subgroup or other subgroups where we can really demonstrate a significant benefit

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.080
for patients that I think will help with the uptake.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.320
But we have no insight yet as to what would that be.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.280
We've modeled it extensively.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:15.200
We continue to believe that we've done the right study and are fully powered

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:21.560
for a 20% relative risk reduction in the 70 milligram per DL and higher patient population

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.320
and a 25% relative risk reduction in the 90 milligram per DL patient population.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:33.200
As a reminder, the median level in the study is 108, so we definitely have enrolled

